      ":question/problem": "Solve the following system of equations:\n    \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}-{x}_{3} &=2 \\\\ {x}_{2}-{x}_{3} &=- \\frac{1}{2} \\\\ {x}_{3} &=- \\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The third equation states that ${x}_{3}=- \\frac{1}{2}.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}-(- \\frac{1}{2})=- \\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}=- \\frac{1}{2}-(\\frac{1}{2})=-1.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute ${x}_{2}=-1$ and ${x}_{3}=- \\frac{1}{2}$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+(-1)-(- \\frac{1}{2})=2.\n$$\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=2-(-1)-(\\frac{1}{2})=\\frac{5}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is ${x}_{1}=\\frac{5}{2}$, ${x}_{2}=-1$, and ${x}_{3}=- \\frac{1}{2}.$ In vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n⟨\\frac{5}{2},-1,- \\frac{1}{2}⟩.\n$$",
